message.content:
Here’s how you can invoke the helper to append initialization statements for both **`width`** and **`height`** on your `shape` object:

```ts
// Assuming `shapeStatements` already exists somewhere above:
await functions.addInitializedPropertyStatements({
  statements: shapeStatements,          // <-- the target statement array
  property:   ["width", "height"],      // <-- properties to initialize
  receiver:   "shape"                   // <-- the object whose props get set
});

// After this call, `shapeStatements` now contains:
// [
//   ...existing statements...,
//   ts.factory.createExpressionStatement(
//     ts.factory.createAssignment(
//       ts.factory.createPropertyAccessExpression(ts.factory.createIdentifier("shape"), "width"),
//       /* default value expression */
//     )
//   ),
//   ts.factory.createExpressionStatement(
//     ts.factory.createAssignment(
//       ts.factory.createPropertyAccessExpression(ts.factory.createIdentifier("shape"), "height"),
//       /* default value expression */
//     )
//   )]
// ```

This single line appends two assignment expressions—one for each property—to the end of your `shapeStatements` array. No further manual edits needed!
